# Catalogue visibility rule (Proto Stock DB)

**Source of truth:** `public.products.available_stock` (via Bladerunner cron).

**Storefront reads:** `public.website_stock` only.

**Join:** `products.sku = website_stock.barcode`.

## Automatic behaviour (Postgres trigger + `apply_catalog_visibility_for_barcode`)

| Source stock | Default action |
|---|---|
| `available_stock > 0` | Live on `website_stock` (auto-restore if `archived_by = 'auto-oos'`) |
| `available_stock <= 0` | Archive to `archived_products` with `archived_by = 'auto-oos'` |

## Exceptions (never auto-moved)

- `keep_live_when_oos = true` on the row — stays live when OOS (admin 📌 pin in Product Manager)
- `archived_by = 'new-products'` — dormant New Products pipeline
- Manual archives: `product-manager`, `recycle-bin`, `admin-bulk`

## Admin override

Product Manager → 📌 pin toggles `keep_live_when_oos`. Pinned OOS products remain on the trade site.

## Migrations

- `016_sync_website_from_products.sql` — price/stock sync
- `017_products_auto_sync_trigger.sql` — sync on every `products` write
- `018_auto_catalog_visibility.sql` — auto live/archive rule + keep flag

Do not reintroduce manual-only sync or hardcoded stock `0` in admin adapt functions.
